<article class="article">
<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Couples Parking</h1>
<p>Parking is the skill nobody books a scooter for and everybody uses twenty times a day. In Hanoi, the good news for couples is structural: the 50cc class is the smallest machine on the street, its parking footprint fits where nothing else does, and the city’s habits around scooter parking are tolerant, practical, and easy to learn. At the verified 200,000 VND per day, one small bike parked well is the difference between a day that flows and a day spent circling blocks. The counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien is open 09:00 to 21:00 daily, and its team can point you at the parking culture before your first stop.</p>
<p>This page follows <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/couples-choosing-a-50cc/">choosing a 50cc as a couple</a> in the couples series on the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a>. For prices across the fleet, the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a> carries the verified numbers, and the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a> answers the general rental questions. Parking for two is a small choreography: one person flies the bike into the spot, the other clears the exit, and both keep the day moving. Here is how that works on Hanoi’s streets.</p>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents"><ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Why parking is the hidden skill</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Where couples can park in Hanoi</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Maneuvering two-up into a spot</a></li>
